{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"760f640b2604d7651243e0270bb9761338e538b8fc726cc9dc572e8f5294427d","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler inbound fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","_build_snapshot","jqls_for","get_parent_map","get_comment_map","get_issuelinks_map","projects_store.read_projects","projects_store.resolve_inbound_bridge_fields","apply_inbound_records.py","_inbound_create_write_create_event","_apply_inbound_create","seen_keys","_ACLI_CEILING","SilentTruncationError","bridge_project","repos","jira_key"],"problem_keywords":["multi-project inbound fetch","jql fan-out","source project recording","enrichment passes","bridge_project","inbound tickets"],"propositions":["The inbound fetcher currently processes only a single configured project and issues one JQL pair with one enrichment pass, silently dropping parent/comment/issuelink data for additional projects in multi-project stores.","Inbound-created tickets do not record their source project, leaving bridge_project and repos fields unset.","The fetcher must fan out JQL queries and all three enrichment passes (parent, comment, issuelink maps) across all projects in the store mapping, merging results into a shared deduplicated snapshot.","Inbound tickets must be stamped with bridge_project (derived from the jira key prefix) and repos (from the project's mapping entry) at the CREATE write site.","Per-project truncation ceiling enforcement prevents one busy project from exhausting a shared budget on behalf of other projects."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787315041726885001,"uuid":